        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ayn Rand, Howard Roark\n- Works: The Fountainhead, Atlas Shrugged\n- Concepts: Objectivism\n- Roles: architect, author, protagonist\n\nFacts:\n- Ayn Rand was a Russian-American author.\n- The Fountainhead is a 1943 novel by Ayn Rand.\n- The Fountainhead was Ayn Rand's first major literary success.\n- Howard Roark is the protagonist of The Fountainhead.\n- Howard Roark is an individualistic young architect who designs modernist buildings.\n- Howard Roark refuses to compromise with an architectural establishment that is unwilling to accept innovation.\n- Ayn Rand is known for the best-selling novels The Fountainhead and Atlas Shrugged.\n- Ayn Rand developed a philosophical system called Objectivism.",
